tag noregion_shared;

saved: ?*int = null;

imported_stash() {
    saved = new int[1](1)
}

/* expect compile {|
store.l8:6:13

    saved = new int[1](1)
            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^

imported_stash stores this allocation in global saved. If imported_stash
runs inside a region, saved could retain a pointer to memory freed when
that region ends.

If this value should be retained, declare imported_stash as noregion.
Its callers also need noregion. This prevents those functions from being
called inside a region.

If the allocation is only needed temporarily, keep it local instead of
storing it in longer-lived storage, and use it before its region ends.

|} */
